      <!-- ───────────────────── Lessons ───────────────────── -->
      <section class="cs-wrap cs-section" aria-labelledby="lessons">
        <p class="cs-num">10</p>
        <h2 id="lessons" class="cs-h2">Lessons from Steven Purdy</h2>

        <ol class="cs-lessons">
          <li>
            <h4>Count the labour, not the licences</h4>
            <p>
              The five subscriptions were $10,450 a month. The people working
              around the gaps between them cost nearly three times that. Any
              consolidation case built only on subscription line items
              understates the return badly.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h4>In insurance roofing, the photos decide everything</h4>
            <p>
              Evidence captured at the door and evidence used to build the claim
              have to live in the same place. Every hour spent moving images
              between systems is an hour of exposure on the claim.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h4>Keep what works</h4>
            <p>
              GoHighLevel was performing and was integrated, not replaced.
              Consolidation removes seams, not tools.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h4>Port the number early</h4>
            <p>
              Communication cutover produced the most immediate benefit and the
              least resistance — customers noticed nothing, staff noticed
              everything.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h4>Train by role, not by product</h4>
            <p>
              Reps saw mobile only. Finance saw finance only. Showing everyone
              the whole platform produces confusion, not competence.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h4>Archive aggressively</h4>
            <p>
              Leaving pre-<mark class="cs-ph">DATE</mark> closed jobs behind
              removed years of duplicates and shortened the migration. Old data
              can live in an export.
            </p>
          </li>
        </ol>

        <figure class="cs-quote">
          <blockquote>
            If I did it again, I'd move faster on the pilot and slower on the
            data. We spent weeks arguing about history we've never once needed
            to look up.
          </blockquote>
          <figcaption>
            Steven Purdy<span>District Manager, Modern Roofing</span>
            <mark class="cs-ph cs-ph--quote">Quote pending written approval</mark>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </section>

